cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  A structured corpus of historical Shanghan literature with clauses,
  commentaries and textual variants
abstract: >-
  The first publicly released dataset of the historical citation and
  commentarial system of the Shanghan Lun, and the first openly available corpus
  to align the canonical clauses with their historical commentarial tradition,
  competing manuscript witnesses and inter-textual relations as separate,
  individually addressable and provenance-tracked layers. Release 1.0 covers 57
  catalogued historical works (425 source text files, 4,763,991 characters) and
  links 398 canonical clauses and 283 auxiliary clauses to 2,958 aligned
  historical commentaries, 616 textual variants and 4,286 inter-textual
  relations. Every structured record resolves to a catalogued work, a source
  text file and a verified SHA-256 checksum. Manual review of the structured
  records is in progress in this version and no agreement statistics are
  reported.
type: dataset
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-11"
license: CC-BY-4.0
